From 425c61161a16274dc3aba6c28bf878df822b8071 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt C <latentcollapse@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 04:53:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 33/45] neurajl: stop a kernel idle for 20 minutes; the next
 call revives it

A finished RLM child is retained for the parent's lifetime, and so was its
kernel: two children in the first 40 minutes of the 12h endurance run left
two idle kernels (about 0.5-0.8 GB each) running. Applies only when state
is saved, so the next call revives what the stopped kernel held.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
